course: dictionary
lesson: 6209
title: Names of places and peoples
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Missouri is a name, so it always starts with a capital letter. It is a proper noun: the name of one particular place or group, not a word for any state or river in general.
explain: Missouri can mean three things: a state in the middle of the USA, a long river, or a Native American people. The clues in the sentence tell you which one. «The Mississippi and its tributaries, such as the Missouri and the Ohio, drain about two-fifths of the 48 neighbouring US states.» Tributaries are rivers that flow into a bigger river, so here Missouri must be a river.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If you think Missouri is a state, try it: «The Missouri flows into the Mississippi» does not make sense for a state, but it does make sense for a river. When the clues are unclear, a map or a dictionary will settle it.
fact: Missouri is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Missouri is a US state in the middle of the country.
fact: The Missouri River is the longest river in North America, and it flows into the Mississippi.
fact: The Missouri are also a Native American people, and the state is named after them.
fact: The nickname of Missouri is the «Show-Me State».
exercise: «The Mississippi and its tributaries, such as the Missouri and the Ohio, drain about two-fifths of the 48 neighbouring US states.» Here, what kind of thing is the Missouri? | A country in Europe | A kind of food | *A river that flows into a bigger river | A month of the year
exercise: What is the nickname of Missouri? | The Empire State | The Lone Star State | *The Show-Me State | The Sunshine State
exercise: Which spelling is correct when Missouri is the name of the state? | misouri | Missuori | *Missouri | missouri
test: Missouri is a state in the middle of which country? | Canada | Australia | *The USA | Brazil
test: The Missouri River flows into which bigger river? | *The Mississippi | The Nile | The Amazon | The Thames
exam: In «The Missouri River flows into the Mississippi», what kind of thing is Missouri? | A sport | A colour | A month | *A river
